/image/6y3zli1mpbduclc/248312e6-469f-481a-9a16-9d55785a4793/91e54400-52d1-11f1-9482-3120031649b2/file-6y3zli1mpbducld.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1mpbduclc/248312e6-469f-481a-9a16-9d55785a4793/91e54400-52d1-11f1-9482-3120031649b2/file-6y3zli1mpbducld.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1mpbduclc/248312e6-469f-481a-9a16-9d55785a4793/91e54400-52d1-11f1-9482-3120031649b2/file-6y3zli1mpbducld.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/6y3zli1mpbduclc/248312e6-469f-481a-9a16-9d55785a4793/91e54400-52d1-11f1-9482-3120031649b2/file-6y3zli1mpbducld.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>In a basic medium, fructose changes (tautomerises) into its isomers, <b>D-glucose</b> and <b>D-mannose</b>. </p>\n<p>Since glucose and mannose are reducing sugars, this explains why fructose also gives a positive test with Fehling’s solution. This solution contains a weak base (dilute NaOH), which allows the reaction to occur.</p>\n<p><b>Option (C)</b></p>\n<p>When sucrose is hydrolysed using an acid, it breaks down into <b>D-glucose</b> and <b>D-fructose</b> in equal amounts (1:1). This mixture is called <b>invert sugar</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Option (D)</b></p>\n<p>The <b>specific rotation</b> of these sugars is as follows:</p>\n<p>For D-fructose: <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.77ex\" height=\"1.785ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 2992.6 789\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"39\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1811,393.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>For D-glucose: <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.77ex\" height=\"1.785ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 2992.6 789\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1811,393.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Therefore, the specific rotation of the invert sugar mixture is the average of the two:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"60.196ex\" height=\"2.755ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -872.7 26606.8 1217.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Specific rotation of invert sugar</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(20077.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(21133.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(21911.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(396.8,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"907.1\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(23336.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(24392.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(25170.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1033,393.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>"}]}